<section class="intro"><p class="eyebrow">A CLEARER WAY TO PLAN</p><h1>A simple plan for every month.</h1><p>Budget Planner helps you compare what you spend and save with your 50/30/20 targets.</p></section>
<div class="help-grid"><section class="panel"><h2>1. Choose your profile and month</h2><p>Create a profile, then choose the month you want to plan. Each profile and month keeps its own income and entries. You can return to earlier months whenever you need.</p><h2>2. Set your take-home income</h2><p>Enter income after taxes and payroll deductions. The planner calculates 50% for needs, 30% for wants, and the remaining 20% for goals. A rounding penny may go to goals so every cent is accounted for.</p></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>3. Record expenses and goals</h2><p><strong>Needs:</strong> essentials such as housing, groceries, utilities, and minimum debt payments.</p><p><strong>Wants:</strong> optional spending such as entertainment, dining out, and hobbies.</p><p><strong>Goals:</strong> savings and extra debt repayments. Record the same payment only once.</p><p>Amounts above needs or wants targets are shown clearly. For goals, the card shows your contributions and how much remains.</p></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>4. Revisit your plan</h2><p>Changes are saved when you choose Save income, Save entry, or Delete. Reopen this app and select the same profile to see your saved data. Changing the month does not move your entries.</p><p>Use Delete to remove a mistaken entry, then add the corrected one.</p></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>Your data stays on this computer</h2><p>This local planner does not connect to a bank. Profiles separate records but do not use passwords; anyone with access to this app can choose a profile.</p><p>If a file cannot be read or a change cannot be saved, the planner shows an error. It does not silently reset unreadable budgets. Back up your data folder; see the README for its location.</p><p>This is a course demonstration of the budgeting method selected for this project.</p></section></div>
